Generalize the equation \(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = x^2y^2\) to a system of equations in three variables where the right-hand side includes a parameter \(k\):
\[
\begin{cases}
x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = x^2y^2, \\
x^2 + z^2 + w^2 = ky^2 + z^2w^2, \\
y^2 + z^2 + w^2 = ky^2w^2.
\end{cases}
\]
Determine if there exist positive integers \(x, y,\) \(z,\) \(w,\) and \(k\) that satisfy all three equations simultaneously.

